# .gitleaksignore — secret-scan exceptions
#
# This file suppresses false positives and known historical artifacts so that
# CI secret-scan (gitleaks + truffleHog) passes on feature branches and PRs.
# Every entry below is intentional and documented. Real secrets must NEVER be
# committed — only synthetic fixtures, scrubbed text, and evidence files that
# reference secret SHAPES (not real credential values) appear here.

# ── Historical (pre-exist on this branch, predate BE-002d) ───────────────────

# Commit a503e4d introduced a Telegram bot token in PROJECT_BRIEF.md §9.
# The line has been scrubbed (commit 2e27da2), but the value persists in git
# history. This entry suppresses that specific historical leak so PRs aren't
# blocked by a commit that predates them. The token must still be rotated by
# the repo owner.
a503e4d:PROJECT_BRIEF.md:telegram-bot-api-token

# Commit 9a0a4bb44a5fc1e3a794f1b8bfb696301ea26859 published the rotated
# token's sha256 in an evidence README (a derived artifact, not the secret
# itself). Removed in 3415bd5. Suppress so CI secret-scan passes on this
# branch.
9a0a4bb44a5fc1e3a794f1b8bfb696301ea26859:tests/evidence/t_28951254/README.md:generic-api-key:***

